<!-- ============ THE FOUR PRESSURES ============ -->
<section class="section" id="dimensions">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where Scale Actually Hurts</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Four pressures, arriving together.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Growth rarely applies in one direction. These are the four that compound — and what absorbs each one.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Pressure One · More Stores</span>
        <h2>Store four hundred behaves like store one.</h2>
        <p>Fleet-wide configuration is set centrally, so opening a location is a configuration task rather than a project. Promotion rules, pricing, permissions, and reporting all inherit from head office.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>Regional promotion groups and rules configured once, inherited everywhere</li>
          <li>Matrixed security rights across hundreds of individual corporate actions</li>
          <li>Employee profile transfers tracked when staff move between locations</li>
          <li><a href="/platform/analytics/" style="color: var(--brand-text);">Unified reporting</a> over the whole estate, not per-store exports stitched together</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="shot-glow"></div>
          <img class="shot-img" src="/assets/images/homepage/cloudhq-kpis.jpg" alt="Cloud HQ reporting across the store estate">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row reverse" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Pressure Two · More Markets</span>
        <h2>A new country is not a new platform.</h2>
        <p>Fiscal and payment requirements are handled inside the platform rather than by a local vendor per territory — which is what usually turns international expansion into a series of one-off implementations.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>Automated fiscal compliance across 40+ countries — VAT, GST, NF525, TSE</li>
          <li>Multi-currency and multi-language, configured per market</li>
          <li>Regional payment methods natively: integrated merchant platforms, QR-based mobile wallets, and market-specific flows such as digital invoicing in China and installment selection in South Korea</li>
          <li>Real-time tax calculation against the destination jurisdiction on shipped orders</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/platform/integrations/" class="btn btn-primary">Integrations &amp; APIs <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="shot-glow"></div>
          <img class="shot-img" src="/assets/images/homepage/analytics-hero.jpg" alt="Retail operations running across international markets">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Pressure Three · More Volume</span>
        <h2>Peak is the only test that counts.</h2>
        <p>Throughput and resilience are properties of the architecture, not of the network you happen to have that day. Selling continues when connectivity does not.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>Store-and-Forward keeps every terminal fully operational through an outage, encrypting locally and syncing on reconnect</li>
          <li><a href="/platform/rfid/" style="color: var(--brand-text);">RFID self-checkout</a> completes a basket in 30 seconds or less, with no item-by-item scanning</li>
          <li>Full-store counts in about 20 minutes instead of 24–48 labor hours</li>
          <li>Add or remove terminals as demand moves — a pop-up counter or 20+ positions across a venue</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="shot-glow"></div>
          <img class="shot-img" src="/assets/images/homepage/rfid-self-checkout.jpg" alt="RFID self-checkout reading a full basket at once">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row reverse" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Pressure Four · More People</span>
        <h2>Every new hire is a scaling event.</h2>
        <p>Headcount grows with store count, and turnover never stops. Onboarding has to be a property of the system rather than a manager's afternoon.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>Role-based <a href="/features/training/" style="color: var(--brand-text);">training</a> assigned automatically from the team member record</li>
          <li>Course material synced from live product data, so nobody learns last season's catalog</li>
          <li>Rotating QR logins and multi-user facial recognition on shared devices — no shared passwords to manage across a fleet</li>
          <li>Company-owned and personal devices governed side by side, with policy per device type</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/features/access-identity/" class="btn btn-primary">Access &amp; identity <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="shot-glow"></div>
          <img class="shot-img" src="/assets/images/homepage/teammate-hero.jpg" alt="Store associates using the platform on their phones">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

